* Halo, in plain words
** The problem
*** Someone did a very long job for you
*** Checking it yourself takes just as long
*** And the job keeps growing every day

** The chain of stamps
*** Each stamp says "my step is right and the last stamp was real"
*** You only look at the newest stamp
*** Every stamp is the same small size

** The sealed envelope
*** Lock a whole formula inside one small fingerprint
*** Prove things about it without opening it
*** The lock is built from public numbers, no secret ceremony

** The library game
*** Ask "left half or right half" over and over
*** About twenty questions for a million books
*** One slow step is left at the very end

** The heavy scale
*** The last check weighs every book on the path
*** As slow as reading the whole library
*** This is the step Halo refuses to pay each time

** Passing the IOU
*** Write a note instead of paying
*** Merge the new note into the old one
*** The note never gets bigger
*** The last person pays once, for everyone

** Two friendly currencies
*** Tweedledum and Tweedledee accept each other's money
*** Steps take turns between the two
*** No exchange fee at any border
*** Ordinary 255-bit curves, nothing exotic

** Results
*** Final proof about 3.5 kilobytes
*** Chain length: as long as you like
*** No secret setup ceremony to trust
*** A big quantum computer would break it
@endmindmap
